and pair potential (B9-B9) intact. This maximizes my waiting tiles including B3 (1 left), B6 (though 0 left), and maintains flexibility.\n\nReason: Discarding B8 removes an isolated tile that doesn't connect well with my hand structure. It preserves the B2-B3-B3-B4-B5 sequence potential and the B9-B9 pair, giving me the best chance to wait for winning tiles like B3 or complete sequences with the connected lower tiles.\n\nAnswer: Play B8"}
